-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-181999/field-2/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-181999/field-2/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" "q-181999/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" "q-181999/field-2/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" "q-181999/field-2/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" "q-181999/field-2/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181999" :question/id #uuid "6966f4d8-cdcd-5ca4-b362-30814d3591d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-181999" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/c7f7b1dc9bf4da61b573345aaf92fe0d29ea00ef5558a9fca985d8af25fa0a03.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny>2.\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181999/field-1" "q-181999/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-182016/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539